Package: miadi-termux
Version: 0.4.0
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: miadi-terminal, miadi-tide, tmux, git, openssh, gh, curl, jq, ripgrep, rsync, nodejs-lts, python, termux-api, termux-services, ffmpeg, fluidsynth, sox
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit
Description: Sets up a Termux phone for the Miadi factory
 The Termux counterpart of the miadi umbrella: one apt install brings what a
 Miadi phone runs. tmux for every session and service, git, openssh and gh
 for the repositories, Node.js and Python for the Miadi tools, termux-api
 and termux-services for Android and services, ffmpeg, fluidsynth and sox
 for recordings and scores, miadi-terminal for clickable chronicle
 references, and miadi-tide for the tide runtime with its daemon in tmux.
 Before every `apt update` it builds the Termux packages the kit's
 origin/main has and this phone's Miadi Termux repository lacks, so
 `apt update && apt upgrade` installs what was pushed to the kit.
 After every dpkg run, when Python moved to another minor version, it runs
 the python-moved hooks that rebuild what was built for the old one.
 Claude Code comes separately, from the claude-code-termux launcher.
